1
00:00:00,216 --> 00:00:01,216
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,216 --> 00:00:02,216
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,216 --> 00:00:03,949
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:56,183 --> 00:00:59,316
[Episode 5]

5
00:01:03,408 --> 00:01:05,968
Honey, what are you doing?

6
00:01:05,968 --> 00:01:07,884
Oh? You're already up?

7
00:01:07,884 --> 00:01:09,549
Why don't you sleep a little longer?

8
00:01:09,549 --> 00:01:12,200
What is it? Are you making breakfast?

9
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,016
No, sit down first.

10
00:01:14,016 --> 00:01:15,240
Huh?

11
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:18,780
I woke up early for once,
so I thought I'd show off my skills.

12
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:20,749
Wow, really?

13
00:01:23,756 --> 00:01:29,383
This boiled egg is just like you,
honest, plain, and exactly as it is.

14
00:01:29,383 --> 00:01:33,532
This good-looking fried egg
is just like me, rich and savory,

15
00:01:33,532 --> 00:01:35,449
with a drizzle of sesame oil.

16
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:40,120
These scrambled eggs are tiny and cute,

17
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:43,348
loaded with butter and milk,
just like our Yul.

18
00:01:43,348 --> 00:01:46,036
It's all eggs, isn't it?

19
00:01:46,036 --> 00:01:47,783
No, it's not.

20
00:01:49,492 --> 00:01:50,504
Ta-da!

21
00:01:50,504 --> 00:01:52,832
This colorful salad and sandwich,

22
00:01:52,832 --> 00:01:56,096
with all three of our
unique personalities together.

23
00:01:56,096 --> 00:01:58,784
Wow, my husband is the best, huh?

24
00:01:58,784 --> 00:02:01,012
When did you make all this by yourself?

25
00:02:01,012 --> 00:02:03,464
Your mom would faint if she found out.

26
00:02:03,464 --> 00:02:06,312
Gosh, she can never find out.

27
00:02:06,312 --> 00:02:10,483
How am I supposed to
weather the storm if she does?

28
00:02:11,876 --> 00:02:14,583
You seem to be in a really
good mood today, honey.

29
00:02:14,583 --> 00:02:15,583
Of course, I am.

30
00:02:15,583 --> 00:02:20,532
I have the two most precious treasures
in the world right here beside me.

31
00:02:20,532 --> 00:02:22,492
And speaking of that...

32
00:02:22,492 --> 00:02:24,020
Mommy!

33
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,236
Yul, are you up?

34
00:02:25,236 --> 00:02:26,684
Is my baby girl awake?

35
00:02:26,684 --> 00:02:28,616
Did you sleep well?

36
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,344
Daddy made all this breakfast
for you and Mommy. See?

37
00:02:32,344 --> 00:02:35,616
- Let's eat quickly.
- Yay! I'll dig in with Kkongsoon.

38
00:02:35,616 --> 00:02:37,316
Okay.

39
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,149
Kkongsoon?

40
00:02:44,752 --> 00:02:48,483
When did we get a new member
of the family without me knowing?

41
00:02:51,072 --> 00:02:53,012
Yul! Look at this!

42
00:02:53,012 --> 00:02:55,774
Your mommy's friend
sent you a doll as a gift.

43
00:02:55,774 --> 00:02:57,016
Mommy, give it to me.

44
00:02:57,016 --> 00:02:58,749
Here.

45
00:03:00,244 --> 00:03:01,800
Oh, I'm jealous.

46
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,883
You have a friend who even
sends you gifts from overseas.

47
00:03:04,883 --> 00:03:07,016
Indeed, having good friends is nice.

48
00:03:07,016 --> 00:03:09,660
Oh, that Russian friend you're close to?

49
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:11,583
Is the name Seul Gi?

50
00:03:11,583 --> 00:03:12,852
Yeah, that's right, Seul Gi.

51
00:03:12,852 --> 00:03:14,632
Come to think of it,
I've never even seen this friend's face.

52
00:03:14,632 --> 00:03:17,149
Seul Gi couldn't come to
our wedding either, right?

53
00:03:17,149 --> 00:03:19,876
I'll introduce you
when Seul Gi comes to Korea.

54
00:03:19,876 --> 00:03:22,276
Anyway, I'm grateful to that friend.

55
00:03:22,276 --> 00:03:24,586
Please send Seul Gi my thanks, double for me.

56
00:03:24,586 --> 00:03:26,649
I already did right after I got it.

57
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:33,916
How's the weather over there these days?

58
00:03:33,916 --> 00:03:36,560
Does it rain on and off?

59
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,940
How are you holding up?

60
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:41,084
You've always hated rain
ever since you were little.

61
00:03:41,084 --> 00:03:43,716
You used to be scared
of thunder and lightning.

62
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:59,483
If you do this one more time,
I'll deep-fry you with a lightning bolt.

63
00:04:06,184 --> 00:04:08,249
Yul, you shouldn't do that.

64
00:04:08,249 --> 00:04:09,416
Yul, you need to eat this.

65
00:04:09,416 --> 00:04:10,583
No, you can't.

66
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:14,032
Yul, you have to eat!

67
00:04:14,032 --> 00:04:15,556
You need to eat your food.

68
00:04:15,556 --> 00:04:17,949
I'm going to catch you, Yul!

69
00:04:21,992 --> 00:04:24,516
[Not Today]

70
00:04:37,156 --> 00:04:38,483
[Caller ID Restricted:
You keep your promises well]

71
00:04:38,483 --> 00:04:40,183
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]

72
00:04:46,808 --> 00:04:49,868
<i>Given that Pyo Kyu Cheol
was also killed by a sniper,</i>

73
00:04:49,868 --> 00:04:51,749
<i>should we conclude that the previous
Jeonjak-dong Hotel incident</i>

74
00:04:51,749 --> 00:04:54,796
- <i>was also the work of Kingfisher?</i>
- Oh, my, I knew it was too quiet.

75
00:04:54,796 --> 00:04:56,849
[Can Kingfisher's Return Be Confirmed?]
<i>Of course. Otherwise, how could</i>

76
00:04:56,849 --> 00:04:59,308
- <i>a string of gun murders happen</i>
- You're here?

77
00:04:59,308 --> 00:05:01,283
- <i>in South Korea?</i>
- It was quiet for a few days.

78
00:05:01,283 --> 00:05:04,212
- <i>So, the return of Kingfisher is confirmed.</i>
- And now it's dominating the headlines.

79
00:05:04,212 --> 00:05:08,283
At times like this,
whatever article I write gets buried.

80
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,904
Whatever I say gets drowned out.

81
00:05:10,904 --> 00:05:15,156
He doesn't even listen to me.
Whatever I say gets buried.

82
00:05:15,156 --> 00:05:16,732
Hey, wait up!

83
00:05:16,732 --> 00:05:21,320
Hey, I heard someone fell
to their death at a construction site.

84
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:23,849
Oh, my. How did that happen?

85
00:05:23,849 --> 00:05:27,232
The chief wants me to
look into what happened.

86
00:05:27,232 --> 00:05:28,716
Apparently, someone sent in a tip.

87
00:05:28,716 --> 00:05:32,260
"It was an unjust death, reveal the truth,"
and all that nonsense.

88
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:34,249
Really?

89
00:05:35,388 --> 00:05:39,684
Then dig deep. Fighting.

90
00:05:39,684 --> 00:05:41,216
Here's what I think.

91
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:42,516
I'd bet this was 100%

92
00:05:42,516 --> 00:05:45,168
an unfortunate accident
caused by safety violations.

93
00:05:45,168 --> 00:05:47,892
If the media starts stirring things up
and digging around,

94
00:05:47,892 --> 00:05:50,964
we could end up bringing down
a perfectly good company

95
00:05:50,964 --> 00:05:53,156
and even causing unexpected ripple effects
on our economy, don't you think?

96
00:05:53,156 --> 00:05:55,780
I wish my colleague Go Ji Soon
would stop talking nonsense

97
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:59,749
and be faithful to a reporter's
sense of mission and the press's duty.

98
00:05:59,749 --> 00:06:01,416
Well, I have another thought.

99
00:06:01,416 --> 00:06:03,638
If my colleague, Mr. Kwon,

100
00:06:03,638 --> 00:06:06,788
who is always devoted to
his mission and duty as a reporter,

101
00:06:06,788 --> 00:06:09,764
were to investigate this case in my place,

102
00:06:09,764 --> 00:06:14,283
maybe he could "dig into it
much more thoroughly," right?

103
00:06:16,116 --> 00:06:18,116
That's a good idea, huh?

104
00:06:19,549 --> 00:06:20,956
Good idea...

105
00:06:20,956 --> 00:06:22,656
Hey, seriously?

106
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:27,416
[Seoul Nambu Police Station]
What? A joint investigation?

107
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:32,124
Whose bright idea was this?

108
00:06:32,124 --> 00:06:34,676
We've reached a preliminary agreement
with the station handling the case.

109
00:06:34,676 --> 00:06:37,083
If you just approve it, Chief...

110
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:39,988
I told you not to stir things up.

111
00:06:39,988 --> 00:06:44,152
The Pyo Kyu Cheol case is different
from Kingfisher's usual methods.

112
00:06:44,152 --> 00:06:46,116
If we cooperate,
we might be able to find a lead...

113
00:06:46,116 --> 00:06:50,316
I don't see why you need to do this.

114
00:06:50,316 --> 00:06:54,932
That punk's case is finally off my hands.
My 10-year ulcer is healing.

115
00:06:54,932 --> 00:06:57,812
Everyone else is desperate
to get that burden off their hands.

116
00:06:57,812 --> 00:07:00,649
What makes you so special?

117
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:08,192
Are you aiming for a few ranks'
worth of promotions or something?

118
00:07:08,192 --> 00:07:09,560
That's not it.

119
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,380
Then back off.

120
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:14,180
You know our precinct's performance
is at the bottom this quarter, right?

121
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:17,176
Instead of worrying about
another precinct's case,

122
00:07:17,176 --> 00:07:19,964
you should nab a few more
petty crooks in our own precinct...

123
00:07:19,964 --> 00:07:21,828
Even one...

124
00:07:21,828 --> 00:07:22,836
Huh?

125
00:07:22,836 --> 00:07:24,536
Wait...

126
00:07:25,344 --> 00:07:27,956
That punk's ignoring me while I'm talking.

127
00:07:27,956 --> 00:07:30,020
I told you to back off, okay?

128
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:32,080
Beom!

129
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:37,048
He could say, "Hey, you're that fired up?
Want to suffer a bit more?"

130
00:07:37,048 --> 00:07:39,448
He knows I'll just suffer with no results.

131
00:07:39,448 --> 00:07:41,976
We're not even asking for more personnel.

132
00:07:41,976 --> 00:07:44,816
The Chief is just doing his job.

133
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:51,384
Why didn't you mention the accidental deaths
of those child sex offenders?

134
00:07:51,384 --> 00:07:53,712
There's no solid evidence.
It's all speculation.

135
00:07:53,712 --> 00:07:57,884
You said you weren't sure if we'd been
barking up the wrong tree or not.

136
00:07:57,884 --> 00:08:01,896
If we're wrong, the eight prior
accidental deaths were all coincidences.

137
00:08:01,896 --> 00:08:05,112
I still can't make sense of it,
even after thinking it over all night.

138
00:08:05,112 --> 00:08:06,349
But if we were right?

139
00:08:06,349 --> 00:08:09,328
Then all the prior deaths were accidents,
and this one was a shooting.

140
00:08:09,328 --> 00:08:10,548
Why on earth?

141
00:08:10,548 --> 00:08:12,128
Why only this time?

142
00:08:12,128 --> 00:08:14,484
Maybe they planned for it to look like
an accident, but something went wrong,

143
00:08:14,484 --> 00:08:16,988
and they had to finish the job with a sniper.

144
00:08:16,988 --> 00:08:20,516
Wow, if that's the case...

145
00:08:20,516 --> 00:08:25,983
Sniping isn't the only method
Kingfisher uses.

146
00:08:25,983 --> 00:08:29,083
Wow, this is getting big.

147
00:08:29,749 --> 00:08:30,983
What are you going to do now?

148
00:08:30,983 --> 00:08:33,583
The chief is making a huge fuss
about telling us to back off, isn't he?

149
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,756
You're here?

150
00:08:42,756 --> 00:08:45,316
That guy sent a gift from Russia.

151
00:08:50,032 --> 00:08:52,172
That guy's sticky fingers are still the same.

152
00:08:52,172 --> 00:08:54,283
Russian-made stuff is pretty useful.

153
00:08:57,004 --> 00:08:59,036
Let's see if there's
anything worth salvaging.

154
00:08:59,036 --> 00:09:00,846
Looks like that guy's gotten restless again.

155
00:09:00,846 --> 00:09:03,116
I heard that the guy
will be coming to Korea soon.

156
00:09:03,116 --> 00:09:06,068
Gosh, I hate seeing that face.

157
00:09:06,068 --> 00:09:10,584
Yeah? Then I'll have to make sure you don't.

158
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:14,300
Wow, this thing is still alive? Huh?

159
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:17,732
I thought it'd suffocate
and die within a few days.

160
00:09:17,732 --> 00:09:20,444
Did you give it some water?

161
00:09:20,444 --> 00:09:23,383
It couldn't have been you taking care of it.

162
00:09:24,044 --> 00:09:26,116
Whoever it was, I'm grateful.

163
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:32,312
I guess you're alive thanks to this guy, huh?

164
00:09:32,312 --> 00:09:34,744
You've worked hard for three years,
air-purifying plant.

165
00:09:34,744 --> 00:09:36,083
It's Tae Soon.

166
00:09:36,083 --> 00:09:38,549
It's even fresh and lively.

167
00:09:40,496 --> 00:09:44,556
You really have no concept of time,
now or then...

168
00:09:44,556 --> 00:09:47,883
It's April, you know. April.

169
00:09:49,328 --> 00:09:52,972
Being trapped in here like this,
I guess even I would lose track of time...

170
00:09:52,972 --> 00:09:54,849
April...

171
00:09:56,644 --> 00:09:58,472
April...

172
00:09:58,472 --> 00:09:59,792
[Client Meeting Pre-Briefing]

173
00:09:59,792 --> 00:10:01,812
His name is Tak Jong Gu.

174
00:10:01,812 --> 00:10:05,812
His dad is a five-term congressman,
and his mom is a chaebol heiress.

175
00:10:05,812 --> 00:10:08,683
He's the notorious youngest son
of the so-called Royal Family.

176
00:10:08,683 --> 00:10:10,192
[Client Information: Personal Details]

177
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:11,336
Let's have something good to drink.

178
00:10:11,336 --> 00:10:13,036
Something fun.

179
00:10:13,936 --> 00:10:17,476
<i>He drugged women, sexually assaulted them,</i>

180
00:10:17,476 --> 00:10:20,228
<i>and even filmed and distributed the footage.</i>

181
00:10:20,228 --> 00:10:23,780
<i>Dozens of videos were found on his computer,</i>

182
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:27,583
<i>yet he got off with
just a two-year suspended sentence.</i>

183
00:10:28,364 --> 00:10:29,816
A suspended sentence?

184
00:10:29,816 --> 00:10:34,516
He had lawyers from a major law firm
settle with the victims one by one.

185
00:10:34,516 --> 00:10:37,944
Settlement is one way to put it.
It was probably money and threats.

186
00:10:37,944 --> 00:10:39,756
Right now, he's holed up
at the Hongseon casino,

187
00:10:39,756 --> 00:10:42,436
gambling away merrily.

188
00:10:42,436 --> 00:10:44,932
So the Gold class is the type with
a lot of money and connections, huh?

189
00:10:44,932 --> 00:10:46,664
The kind who can wriggle out of anything
despite their crimes.

190
00:10:46,664 --> 00:10:48,983
They're the biggest headache.

191
00:10:49,636 --> 00:10:52,349
They're usually heavily guarded,
so getting close to them isn't easy.

192
00:10:52,349 --> 00:10:54,208
And it doesn't come cheap, either.

193
00:10:54,208 --> 00:10:56,452
Especially when we're barely
keeping our operating expenses afloat.

194
00:10:56,452 --> 00:10:58,192
- A casino?
- Yeah.

195
00:10:58,192 --> 00:11:02,952
His dad is aiming to become
National Assembly Speaker in a month.

196
00:11:02,952 --> 00:11:05,368
So he was given strict orders to lie low

197
00:11:05,368 --> 00:11:08,604
somewhere out of the public eye until then.

198
00:11:08,604 --> 00:11:11,368
Tak Jong Gu is easily excitable
and has weak self-control.

199
00:11:11,368 --> 00:11:14,688
So he's susceptible to gambling addiction.

200
00:11:14,688 --> 00:11:16,700
[Client Information: Criminal History]
He has no sense of guilt, either.

201
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,844
<i>Five years ago, a woman in her twenties</i>

202
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:21,383
<i>fell to her death from a high-rise apartment.</i>

203
00:11:21,383 --> 00:11:24,416
<i>Tak Jong Gu was there too.</i>

204
00:11:25,028 --> 00:11:26,568
Darn it.

205
00:11:26,568 --> 00:11:28,316
Why were you acting up?

206
00:11:28,316 --> 00:11:30,683
How did he get away with it back then?

207
00:11:32,604 --> 00:11:37,188
He claimed they had a fight and that
she impulsively jumped to her death.

208
00:11:37,188 --> 00:11:41,983
The court acquitted him
due to insufficient evidence.

209
00:11:44,292 --> 00:11:46,504
This one's quite an upgrade, huh?

210
00:11:46,504 --> 00:11:48,049
Seems like the world's
getting easier to push around.

211
00:11:48,049 --> 00:11:50,216
[Tak Jong Gu's social media post:
The world is on my side again]

212
00:11:50,216 --> 00:11:51,216
[Law can go to the dogs]

213
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:55,556
Alright, he's holed up in the provinces.

214
00:11:55,556 --> 00:11:58,128
We'll have to go on a business trip.

215
00:11:58,128 --> 00:12:01,183
These days, faking an accidental death

216
00:12:01,183 --> 00:12:03,964
with some half-baked scenario
just won't cut it.

217
00:12:03,964 --> 00:12:07,332
We're living in the age of
cutting-edge forensics.

218
00:12:07,332 --> 00:12:11,884
Oh, coming up with a scenario
for every meeting is the hardest part.

219
00:12:11,884 --> 00:12:17,116
Figuring out how to kill someone is
harder than figuring out how to save them.

220
00:12:19,576 --> 00:12:21,516
I'll handle this one.

221
00:12:22,444 --> 00:12:24,144
You will, Director Yoo?

222
00:12:25,416 --> 00:12:29,724
But considering the unexpected
Pyo Kyu Cheol incident

223
00:12:29,724 --> 00:12:32,388
stirred up the media and police,

224
00:12:32,388 --> 00:12:36,149
wouldn't it be risky to do
another one right away?

225
00:12:39,368 --> 00:12:43,104
If we're doing it, I hope we hit the jackpot
on the meeting day.

226
00:12:43,104 --> 00:12:47,949
Make the day of greatest joy
become his ancestral rite day, right?

227
00:12:52,976 --> 00:12:54,676
Ancestral rite...

228
00:12:57,260 --> 00:12:58,983
What day is it today?

229
00:13:01,008 --> 00:13:03,983
[Mother]

230
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,716
Hello, Mother.

231
00:13:12,492 --> 00:13:15,252
Of course, I know.

232
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:16,952
Yeah.

233
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,720
Assistant Manager Yang,
I still have my half-day off, right?

234
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:29,349
Please. We'll continue
the meeting tomorrow. Sorry.

235
00:13:34,836 --> 00:13:37,860
Director Yoo must attend
the ancestral rite at her in-laws' house.

236
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:39,216
Of course, she does.
She's the daughter-in-law.

237
00:13:39,216 --> 00:13:41,648
So Kingfisher has become
a daughter-in-law now too.

238
00:13:41,648 --> 00:13:43,408
On a day like this, isn't she less
a daughter-in-law and more a servant?

239
00:13:43,408 --> 00:13:45,583
I should probably come with her...

240
00:14:04,592 --> 00:14:05,849
I think this is the place.

241
00:14:05,849 --> 00:14:11,483
[My Safety, My Coworkers' Safety]

242
00:14:16,204 --> 00:14:18,250
<i>Two weeks ago, a worker fell to his death</i>

243
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:20,424
<i>while organizing materials
on the sixth floor.</i>

244
00:14:20,424 --> 00:14:22,432
<i>The investigation concluded
that it was an accident</i>

245
00:14:22,432 --> 00:14:25,757
<i>caused by his own negligence, correct?</i>

246
00:14:25,757 --> 00:14:28,116
That's what's been made public.

247
00:14:28,116 --> 00:14:29,312
Now we need to find out for ourselves.

248
00:14:29,312 --> 00:14:34,849
Whether it was just an accident
or an unjust death disguised as one.

249
00:14:34,849 --> 00:14:37,272
While everyone's
focused on the Kingfisher case,

250
00:14:37,272 --> 00:14:38,700
we'll investigate the unjust death of

251
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:42,549
the socially vulnerable
left in the blind spot?

252
00:14:43,949 --> 00:14:45,868
I really like this kind of stuff.

253
00:14:45,868 --> 00:14:48,716
This is what being a reporter is all about.

254
00:14:48,716 --> 00:14:50,449
Let's go, Mr. Kwon.

255
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,948
I mean, the police already came and went.

256
00:14:59,948 --> 00:15:03,588
The Ministry of Employment and Labor
and the Ministry of Land investigated too.

257
00:15:03,588 --> 00:15:07,336
It was all determined
to be personal negligence.

258
00:15:07,336 --> 00:15:11,952
Really? Then what were the names
of the officials who came out that day?

259
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:14,383
Well, still, our chairman said

260
00:15:14,383 --> 00:15:17,680
the company had a moral obligation,
so we covered workers' compensation,

261
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:22,249
the death benefit, and even added
a hefty condolence payment.

262
00:15:22,249 --> 00:15:28,048
There's no one as generous as our chairman.

263
00:15:28,048 --> 00:15:29,456
I see.

264
00:15:29,456 --> 00:15:33,649
I'll ask the chairman about that myself.
Where can I meet him?

265
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:38,860
Well, it's rather difficult
to meet the chairman in person.

266
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:43,192
Then what about the coworkers who worked
with the deceased, Kang Yeong Ho?

267
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:45,312
Oh, that's possible.

268
00:15:45,312 --> 00:15:46,752
Oh, there's one right over there.

269
00:15:46,752 --> 00:15:49,383
- Mr. Park Chun Bok!
- Yes.

270
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,916
Go talk to him.

271
00:15:57,700 --> 00:16:01,368
That fellow Kang Yeong Ho,
he reeked of alcohol that day.

272
00:16:01,368 --> 00:16:06,012
I don't know if he'd been drinking
all morning or was still hungover.

273
00:16:06,012 --> 00:16:08,271
It had happened a few times before too.

274
00:16:08,271 --> 00:16:11,983
That day too, he didn't wear his hard hat,
so I warned him several times.

275
00:16:11,983 --> 00:16:13,824
Yeah.

276
00:16:13,824 --> 00:16:15,148
I see.

277
00:16:15,148 --> 00:16:19,043
Did you report that to the company as well?

278
00:16:19,043 --> 00:16:23,583
Do you think I feel good talking about
a former colleague like that?

279
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:25,568
Besides, he's dead.

280
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:28,764
Still, I thought I should be honest
about what happened.

281
00:16:28,764 --> 00:16:31,804
- Yeah.
- Of course, you should have.

282
00:16:31,804 --> 00:16:35,900
Even after all that, the chairman
was incredibly generous, wasn't he?

283
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:37,206
Yeah.

284
00:16:37,206 --> 00:16:40,216
So everyone seems pretty grateful
to the chairman.

285
00:16:40,216 --> 00:16:42,660
We were at a loss
because the construction was delayed too.

286
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:47,049
The chairman even made sure
we got our wages in advance.

287
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:56,204
I mean, the company
processed the industrial accident,

288
00:16:56,204 --> 00:16:58,928
paid the compensation,
and even gave a condolence payment.

289
00:16:58,928 --> 00:17:01,856
Didn't they do everything
they were supposed to?

290
00:17:01,856 --> 00:17:05,104
That's not something companies usually do.

291
00:17:05,104 --> 00:17:06,918
You know it well.

292
00:17:06,918 --> 00:17:08,016
Pardon?

293
00:17:08,016 --> 00:17:12,104
He smelled of alcohol
and wasn't wearing a hard hat.

294
00:17:12,104 --> 00:17:13,344
In such cases, companies usually

295
00:17:13,344 --> 00:17:15,816
highlight personal negligence
and cut ties without mercy.

296
00:17:15,816 --> 00:17:17,849
That's how companies operate.

297
00:17:18,508 --> 00:17:23,016
But the chairman stepped in
and went all out with compensation?

298
00:17:23,016 --> 00:17:27,992
And this so-called witness
just happens to show up

299
00:17:27,992 --> 00:17:30,660
and start talking about
the victim's negligence.

300
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:33,176
Oh, you're right.

301
00:17:33,176 --> 00:17:34,784
So what do we do now?

302
00:17:34,784 --> 00:17:36,724
We don't even know
who the informant is, do we?

303
00:17:36,724 --> 00:17:38,424
Well, that's...

304
00:17:40,249 --> 00:17:42,432
[Receive Gaecheon Construction
Meal Tickets Here]

305
00:17:42,432 --> 00:17:45,316
Let's grab some food first
and look into it afterward.

306
00:17:45,316 --> 00:17:48,449
We're eating again?
We just ate before we came.

307
00:17:52,308 --> 00:17:54,724
- Take a look before you go.
- I'll be right back.

308
00:17:54,724 --> 00:17:57,400
- Yeah.
- It's been a while.

309
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,104
You know we're not serving
steamed rice cake, right?

310
00:17:59,104 --> 00:18:01,806
- You're here?
- Oh, really? Hello.

311
00:18:01,806 --> 00:18:03,668
Hey, I'm here.

312
00:18:03,668 --> 00:18:05,416
Oh, Tae Seong's family is here.

313
00:18:05,416 --> 00:18:06,549
The baby's mom came too?

314
00:18:06,549 --> 00:18:07,964
Yeah, have you been well?

315
00:18:07,964 --> 00:18:09,068
Welcome.

316
00:18:09,068 --> 00:18:13,716
Seeing you bring your daughter-in-law,
it must be an ancestral rite day.

317
00:18:13,716 --> 00:18:17,088
Don't make that delicate daughter-in-law
do all the work every time.

318
00:18:17,088 --> 00:18:18,752
Bring that precious son of yours too.

319
00:18:18,752 --> 00:18:21,374
Oh, please. Why would my son come here?

320
00:18:21,374 --> 00:18:23,591
He's busy working at the company.

321
00:18:23,591 --> 00:18:27,072
Anyway, you're always going on
about your son, all year round.

322
00:18:27,072 --> 00:18:30,160
So, what kind of fish are you making?

323
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:34,140
- Hey, you pick one out.
- What?

324
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:37,649
Pick out what you think we should buy.

325
00:18:38,956 --> 00:18:41,649
Oh, okay.

326
00:18:46,544 --> 00:18:47,556
How about this, Mother?

327
00:18:47,556 --> 00:18:48,780
Oh, my.

328
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,790
- Oh, what am I going to do?
- It's so shiny.

329
00:18:50,790 --> 00:18:52,748
Oh, jeez.

330
00:18:52,748 --> 00:18:56,583
Hey, I told you clearly that fish
whose names end in "chi" are low-grade

331
00:18:56,583 --> 00:19:00,385
and shouldn't go on
the memorial table, didn't I?

332
00:19:00,385 --> 00:19:03,470
How can you keep doing this
when I've told you so many times?

333
00:19:03,470 --> 00:19:05,908
Oh, jeez.

334
00:19:05,908 --> 00:19:08,349
She never told me that.

335
00:19:10,588 --> 00:19:14,383
I'm sorry, Mother. I'll make sure
to remember from now on.

336
00:19:14,383 --> 00:19:19,483
Then, among the ones
that don't end in "chi"...

337
00:19:20,482 --> 00:19:21,776
This is a croaker, right?

338
00:19:21,776 --> 00:19:23,800
Yeah, croaker!

339
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:26,183
This one's saury?

340
00:19:27,144 --> 00:19:28,832
And that one is mackerel?

341
00:19:28,832 --> 00:19:30,264
And this one's pomfret!

342
00:19:30,264 --> 00:19:31,816
Am I right, Mother?

343
00:19:31,816 --> 00:19:35,683
Oh, my, now you know it perfectly
without even being told?

344
00:19:35,683 --> 00:19:38,920
So, we can't have saury and mackerel,
which end in "chi,"

345
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:42,516
so please give me pomfret and croaker,
which don't end in "chi."

346
00:19:42,516 --> 00:19:43,620
Oh, okay.

347
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,883
- And some abalone too.
- Okay.

348
00:19:53,816 --> 00:19:56,784
Kang Yeong Ho? He was drinking?

349
00:19:56,784 --> 00:19:59,536
Oh, my, where did you hear such nonsense?

350
00:19:59,536 --> 00:20:03,271
Right? See? I told you it wasn't true.

351
00:20:03,271 --> 00:20:06,120
- Pardon?
- I mean, she kept insisting that

352
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:07,820
everyone at the construction site drinks,

353
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:12,216
and that Kang Yeong Ho caused the accident
because he was still drunk that day.

354
00:20:14,483 --> 00:20:16,283
Oh, that's right. I remember now.

355
00:20:16,283 --> 00:20:19,532
I had a bit of a preconceived notion.

356
00:20:19,532 --> 00:20:22,516
You shouldn't make someone
so wrongfully accused like that.

357
00:20:22,516 --> 00:20:25,249
That man never even touched alcohol.

358
00:20:25,249 --> 00:20:30,720
Even when he had something really upsetting
going on, I never saw him drink.

359
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,984
Something upsetting?

360
00:20:31,984 --> 00:20:36,772
Yeah, I heard something happened to his wife.

361
00:20:36,772 --> 00:20:41,124
That guy absolutely adored his wife.

362
00:20:41,124 --> 00:20:44,208
As they say these days,
he was a total wife guy.

363
00:20:44,208 --> 00:20:48,316
Oh, sounds just like me.

364
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:56,380
Wait, now that I think about it, his wife
used to work at the chairman's house.

365
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:59,183
That's enough, right? Enjoy your meal.

366
00:21:01,996 --> 00:21:03,916
The chairman's house?

367
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:16,132
- Oh, my.
- They're here.

368
00:21:16,132 --> 00:21:18,160
Mommy!

369
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:19,852
Yul, what were you playing?

370
00:21:19,852 --> 00:21:24,340
I was playing with Auntie,
Kkongsoon, and Chiba.

371
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:28,339
Oh, my sister-in-law had to
play pack mule again.

372
00:21:28,339 --> 00:21:30,707
- Jeez!
- Quit nagging and just take the bags.

373
00:21:30,707 --> 00:21:33,983
I'm doing it. I'm doing it.

374
00:21:47,876 --> 00:21:49,496
[Three Years Ago]
Hey!

375
00:21:49,496 --> 00:21:52,061
Have you never chopped an onion before?

376
00:21:52,061 --> 00:21:54,583
Why are you using the knife like that?

377
00:21:54,583 --> 00:21:56,386
Are you cutting a cake or something?

378
00:21:56,386 --> 00:21:59,616
I'm just not used to using it
for this kind of thing.

379
00:22:00,483 --> 00:22:03,916
[Two Years Ago]

380
00:22:05,144 --> 00:22:07,152
Wait, why is this here?

381
00:22:07,152 --> 00:22:10,283
Do we have any Southeast Asian ancestors?

382
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:13,183
I just bought it for you to try.

383
00:22:13,183 --> 00:22:15,380
[One Year Ago]

384
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:16,733
Hey!

385
00:22:16,733 --> 00:22:19,096
Did you mix grains into the rice?

386
00:22:19,096 --> 00:22:21,796
For the rice we're putting
on the memorial table?

387
00:22:21,796 --> 00:22:23,776
They say it's good for your health...

388
00:22:23,776 --> 00:22:28,383
Wow, jeez. You're driving me crazy. Really.

389
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:43,688
Okay!

390
00:22:43,688 --> 00:22:45,388
Should I give it a try?

391
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:04,108
Hey, did you put garlic
in the seasoned vegetables?

392
00:23:04,108 --> 00:23:06,516
Yes, Mother, for a deeper flavor...

393
00:23:07,716 --> 00:23:10,349
Wait... All of that too?

394
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:14,471
Mother, I put it in all of...

395
00:23:14,471 --> 00:23:15,976
I'm sorry, Mother. Oh, no.

396
00:23:15,976 --> 00:23:19,171
Oh, I'll go right now and buy them again.

397
00:23:19,171 --> 00:23:20,576
I'm sorry.

398
00:23:20,576 --> 00:23:23,816
What are we going to do with all this?

399
00:23:24,436 --> 00:23:25,808
I'll be back.

400
00:23:25,808 --> 00:23:27,750
- Wow, seriously...
- Jeez.

401
00:23:27,750 --> 00:23:30,721
Putting garlic
in ancestral rite vegetables...

402
00:23:30,721 --> 00:23:33,159
No matter how clueless she is,
that's too much.

403
00:23:33,159 --> 00:23:36,736
- It's too much, too much.
- Come on. She might not know.

404
00:23:36,736 --> 00:23:38,096
It's no big deal.

405
00:23:38,096 --> 00:23:40,548
It's because she's an orphan.

406
00:23:40,548 --> 00:23:43,548
She never had parents
to teach her these things.

407
00:23:43,548 --> 00:23:45,980
I knew that line was coming.

408
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:48,480
You really found your opening, Mom.

409
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:50,583
Be quiet, you girl!

410
00:23:52,549 --> 00:23:57,516
[Kang Yeong Ho]

411
00:24:01,096 --> 00:24:02,496
<i>Tae Seong, when are you coming?</i>

412
00:24:02,496 --> 00:24:04,196
Is anyone home?

413
00:24:10,504 --> 00:24:12,383
Hello?

414
00:24:14,272 --> 00:24:16,248
I guess no one's here.

415
00:24:16,248 --> 00:24:19,992
Do you really think
Kang Yeong Ho's wife is the informant?

416
00:24:19,992 --> 00:24:21,816
What's the matter?

417
00:24:21,816 --> 00:24:24,508
They moved out. No one lives there now.

418
00:24:24,508 --> 00:24:26,236
They moved? When?

419
00:24:26,236 --> 00:24:28,449
I think it was the day
of the husband's funeral.

420
00:24:28,449 --> 00:24:31,504
They seemed to be in a hurry
and called a moving truck that night.

421
00:24:31,504 --> 00:24:34,356
Do you happen to have
the wife's contact information?

422
00:24:34,356 --> 00:24:36,928
No, we're not close enough
to have each other's numbers.

423
00:24:36,928 --> 00:24:39,340
Is there a real estate office nearby?

424
00:24:39,340 --> 00:24:40,516
A real estate office?

425
00:24:40,516 --> 00:24:42,588
Oh, I guess you're here to look at the house.

426
00:24:42,588 --> 00:24:45,812
Go out of this alley
and turn the corner. It's right there.

427
00:24:45,812 --> 00:24:47,649
Okay, thank you.

428
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:51,396
Why the real estate office?

429
00:24:51,396 --> 00:24:53,816
If she left in such a hurry, she probably
couldn't even get her deposit back.

430
00:24:53,816 --> 00:24:55,183
She'll have to contact them
eventually, right?

431
00:24:55,183 --> 00:24:56,232
What is she talking about?

432
00:24:56,232 --> 00:24:59,132
<i>Bo Na is going through a rough time.
She's become Mom's lackey.</i>

433
00:24:59,132 --> 00:25:01,700
<i>Tae Seong, you didn't forget about
the ancestral rite today, did you?</i>

434
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:02,824
Oh!

435
00:25:02,824 --> 00:25:04,260
What is it? What's wrong, Mr. Kwon?

436
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:05,504
What time is it now?

437
00:25:05,504 --> 00:25:06,824
Right now?

438
00:25:06,824 --> 00:25:08,524
Oh!

439
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:13,683
Oh, my, I can't live
a long life like this. Jeez.

440
00:25:16,216 --> 00:25:17,288
[I'm in Gangwon Province right now,
but I'll get there as soon as I can]

441
00:25:17,288 --> 00:25:19,216
Gangwon Province?

442
00:25:19,216 --> 00:25:22,516
Oh, my, if he leaves now,
when is he supposed to get here?

443
00:25:23,380 --> 00:25:26,249
Auntie, what's an ancestral rite?

444
00:25:27,236 --> 00:25:29,812
Yul, do you want to know
what an ancestral rite is?

445
00:25:29,812 --> 00:25:32,120
An ancestral rite is...

446
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:34,028
when people who have gone to heaven

447
00:25:34,028 --> 00:25:38,488
come over to our house to eat,
have fun, and then go back.

448
00:25:38,488 --> 00:25:40,540
What is an orphan?

449
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:42,240
Huh?

450
00:25:44,472 --> 00:25:48,392
Anyway, Mom said that in front of the child.

451
00:25:48,392 --> 00:25:51,568
That's for parents...

452
00:25:51,568 --> 00:25:57,632
Well, it means Yul's mommy's parents
have passed away.

453
00:25:57,632 --> 00:25:59,949
Is Mommy an orphan?

454
00:26:01,692 --> 00:26:05,916
Yes. Her parents went to heaven
a very long time ago.

455
00:26:05,916 --> 00:26:08,483
Then are they coming over for dinner today?

456
00:26:09,996 --> 00:26:15,148
No. The people coming today are someone else.

457
00:26:15,148 --> 00:26:16,148
Why aren't they coming?

458
00:26:16,148 --> 00:26:19,536
Well... Maybe because they weren't invited?

459
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:20,844
Then when are they coming?

460
00:26:20,844 --> 00:26:22,980
Oh, well...

461
00:26:22,980 --> 00:26:24,680
If you call them?

462
00:26:27,168 --> 00:26:29,796
They'll come if you call them.

463
00:26:29,796 --> 00:26:32,849
Like, "Please come quickly."

464
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:39,116
Yul's mommy!

465
00:26:39,116 --> 00:26:40,984
[Ok's Flower Shop]

466
00:26:40,984 --> 00:26:44,083
- Oh, my, ma'am!
- What brings you here at this hour?

467
00:26:47,024 --> 00:26:49,412
Do you have a minute right now?

468
00:26:49,412 --> 00:26:51,612
- Me?
- Yeah.

469
00:26:51,612 --> 00:26:52,888
Right now?

470
00:26:52,888 --> 00:26:55,896
Well... I have to go.

471
00:26:55,896 --> 00:26:57,949
What's going on? Why?

472
00:27:05,804 --> 00:27:07,449
- I'm here.
- Daddy!

473
00:27:07,449 --> 00:27:08,908
Yul!

474
00:27:08,908 --> 00:27:11,076
What? You got here sooner than I expected.

475
00:27:11,076 --> 00:27:12,268
Did you speed all the way here?

476
00:27:12,268 --> 00:27:13,916
Where's Bo Na?
She wasn't answering her phone.

477
00:27:13,916 --> 00:27:17,280
She's on the veranda. And as you can see,
she couldn't answer the phone.

478
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:18,424
Since the afternoon, all day...

479
00:27:18,424 --> 00:27:20,392
So why was she here all day? What about work?

480
00:27:20,392 --> 00:27:22,304
She took a half-day off.
I guess Mom called her.

481
00:27:22,304 --> 00:27:23,508
Mom's resting in the master bedroom.

482
00:27:23,508 --> 00:27:26,832
- Let's go, Yul! Let's go with Auntie.
- Let's go.

483
00:27:26,832 --> 00:27:29,216
Let's go! Want to draw?

484
00:27:32,740 --> 00:27:35,112
- Honey!
- You're here?

485
00:27:35,112 --> 00:27:38,148
You should have told me.
I almost completely forgot.

486
00:27:38,148 --> 00:27:40,149
Sorry. I forgot too.

487
00:27:41,528 --> 00:27:43,328
Oh, my, really, Mom...

488
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:45,224
Why did she call someone who works
at a company out in the afternoon?

489
00:27:45,224 --> 00:27:47,748
Come on, it's just one day.
Why are you making a fuss?

490
00:27:47,748 --> 00:27:48,888
There's just a little cleanup left.

491
00:27:48,888 --> 00:27:50,404
It's all done. It's all done.

492
00:27:50,404 --> 00:27:51,448
Rest. I'll do it.

493
00:27:51,448 --> 00:27:53,628
No, don't say things like that.
Just sit over there.

494
00:27:53,628 --> 00:27:56,216
I can finish it quickly before Mom comes out.

495
00:27:59,740 --> 00:28:01,636
- Huh?
- Did you get hurt?

496
00:28:01,636 --> 00:28:06,328
Yeah, I scratched myself while cleaning
the abalone earlier. It was bleeding...

497
00:28:06,328 --> 00:28:07,848
Stay right there.

498
00:28:07,848 --> 00:28:10,516
I put some medicine on it. Honey, it's okay.

499
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:15,420
I'm okay.

500
00:28:15,420 --> 00:28:17,283
I'm not okay.

501
00:28:20,260 --> 00:28:22,083
It must hurt.

502
00:28:39,184 --> 00:28:41,392
There, done.

503
00:28:41,392 --> 00:28:43,010
It clings just like skin.

504
00:28:43,010 --> 00:28:46,376
You put it on so well
that it's like it's not even there.

505
00:28:46,376 --> 00:28:48,756
And it's easy to move around with.

506
00:28:48,756 --> 00:28:50,104
Thanks.

507
00:28:50,104 --> 00:28:51,156
I should get back to work.

508
00:28:51,156 --> 00:28:52,516
Oh, I told you, it's fine.

509
00:28:52,516 --> 00:28:54,216
Why?

510
00:28:55,132 --> 00:28:56,204
No.

511
00:28:56,204 --> 00:28:57,764
I can just quickly finish
before Mom comes out.

512
00:28:57,764 --> 00:29:00,464
- I'll get in trouble.
- It's okay.

513
00:29:00,464 --> 00:29:03,216
No, she's scary.

514
00:29:10,116 --> 00:29:12,116
Please get some rest.

515
00:29:24,528 --> 00:29:26,228
Mother!

516
00:29:35,268 --> 00:29:36,916
Let's go. Let's go.

517
00:29:36,916 --> 00:29:37,916
It's Yul!

518
00:29:37,916 --> 00:29:39,956
- Yul!
- Auntie!

519
00:29:39,956 --> 00:29:42,004
- When did you get here?
- Have you been well?

520
00:29:42,004 --> 00:29:43,536
How did you two get here together?

521
00:29:43,536 --> 00:29:45,408
Du Ri stopped by the shop and gave me a ride.

522
00:29:45,408 --> 00:29:47,220
What about you? Where are you taking Yul?

523
00:29:47,220 --> 00:29:50,749
Oh, we're going for a walk to the playground.

524
00:29:50,749 --> 00:29:52,083
Really? Oh, my, that sounds nice.

525
00:29:52,083 --> 00:29:53,647
Go on ahead, okay?

526
00:29:53,647 --> 00:29:57,060
- Be careful.
- Careful, careful.

527
00:29:57,060 --> 00:29:58,568
- Evacuate.
- Evacuate?

528
00:29:58,568 --> 00:29:59,684
- Oh, my.
- Why?

529
00:29:59,684 --> 00:30:02,849
It's obvious. Mom's giving
her daughter-in-law a hard time again.

530
00:30:04,508 --> 00:30:07,216
What's it this time?
What's she unhappy about now?

531
00:30:07,216 --> 00:30:10,683
Tae Seong got caught
doing the dishes in the kitchen.

532
00:30:10,683 --> 00:30:11,683
Oh, my.

533
00:30:11,683 --> 00:30:12,756
What?

534
00:30:12,756 --> 00:30:14,816
Take that off. Take it off.

535
00:30:14,816 --> 00:30:16,149
- I said take it off!
- Oh, I'm done.

536
00:30:16,149 --> 00:30:18,312
Take it off, got it?

537
00:30:18,312 --> 00:30:20,712
Did I raise you like that?

538
00:30:20,712 --> 00:30:24,020
I raised you without ever
making you lift a finger.

539
00:30:24,020 --> 00:30:26,083
I'm sorry, Mother.

540
00:30:26,083 --> 00:30:28,028
- I...
- Mom.

541
00:30:28,028 --> 00:30:30,301
She's been working all day.
I just told her to rest a bit.

542
00:30:30,301 --> 00:30:33,220
How much work could she possibly have done?

543
00:30:33,220 --> 00:30:35,848
Hey, come out. You, come here!

544
00:30:35,848 --> 00:30:40,649
Do you usually make
our Tae Seong do housework?

545
00:30:42,596 --> 00:30:46,944
No, what housework? I do housework?

546
00:30:46,944 --> 00:30:49,549
Bossing him around. You made him.

547
00:30:49,549 --> 00:30:50,988
No wonder.

548
00:30:50,988 --> 00:30:54,044
You looked way too practiced
for this to be your first time.

549
00:30:54,044 --> 00:30:57,504
Last time, too, when she was away
using work as an excuse,

550
00:30:57,504 --> 00:30:59,436
you cooked and cleaned up after her.

551
00:30:59,436 --> 00:31:01,749
I didn't say anything then,
but I was furious.

552
00:31:01,749 --> 00:31:03,816
- Mom! That was me...
- Mom, we're here.

553
00:31:03,816 --> 00:31:05,383
We brought kimchi.

554
00:31:05,383 --> 00:31:06,383
- You're here?
- Guys.

555
00:31:06,383 --> 00:31:08,396
You had a hard time, right?

556
00:31:08,396 --> 00:31:11,449
Good grief, Tae Seong is doing the dishes.

557
00:31:11,449 --> 00:31:14,388
He never once set foot in the kitchen.

558
00:31:14,388 --> 00:31:17,144
Imagine how much pressure
she must've put on him.

559
00:31:17,144 --> 00:31:19,540
Goodness, what on earth is going on?

560
00:31:19,540 --> 00:31:21,084
Mom, she hurt her hand.

561
00:31:21,084 --> 00:31:23,756
How did her perfectly fine hand
suddenly get hurt?

562
00:31:23,756 --> 00:31:24,849
She's faking it
because she doesn't want to work.

563
00:31:24,849 --> 00:31:26,556
You're hurt?

564
00:31:26,556 --> 00:31:28,416
- No, I'm fine.
- You should've been more careful.

565
00:31:28,416 --> 00:31:30,540
- Just a little. This tiny bit.
- Oh, dear.

566
00:31:30,540 --> 00:31:32,683
- Are you okay?
- Now that we're all gathered.

567
00:31:34,252 --> 00:31:37,836
Let's settle this once and for all.

568
00:31:37,836 --> 00:31:40,228
- What?
- Here's what I think.

569
00:31:40,228 --> 00:31:42,484
Settle what?
Honey, what are you talking about?

570
00:31:42,484 --> 00:31:44,520
- Don't do this.
- I think that...

571
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:45,650
it's our family's ancestral rite,

572
00:31:45,650 --> 00:31:47,224
yet you're making
the daughter-in-law do all the work?

573
00:31:47,224 --> 00:31:49,608
I think this is unfair.

574
00:31:49,608 --> 00:31:53,283
Times have changed,
so men should help out too.

575
00:31:53,283 --> 00:31:55,076
And she's going back to work now too.

576
00:31:55,076 --> 00:31:58,648
So, from now on, I'll come early
and help out more. Okay?

577
00:31:58,648 --> 00:32:00,776
- No.
- What a load of nonsense.

578
00:32:00,776 --> 00:32:02,468
Who says anyone's doing anything?

579
00:32:02,468 --> 00:32:03,592
Jeez.

580
00:32:03,592 --> 00:32:08,368
Why are you suddenly acting like this
when you've always listened to Mom?

581
00:32:08,368 --> 00:32:10,085
And from now on,
you should come early and help too.

582
00:32:10,085 --> 00:32:12,960
Don't leave it all to Bo Na.

583
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:15,283
Kwon Tae Seong, you're being ridiculous.

584
00:32:15,283 --> 00:32:17,712
Sun Il, that's not what he...

585
00:32:17,712 --> 00:32:18,712
Oh, I'm sorry.

586
00:32:18,712 --> 00:32:21,364
It's fine when Mom and your sisters
work themselves to death,

587
00:32:21,364 --> 00:32:24,816
but you can't stand
seeing your wife struggle?

588
00:32:24,816 --> 00:32:27,616
- That's not what I meant...
- Oh, both of you, stop it.

589
00:32:27,616 --> 00:32:29,892
Tae Seong isn't wrong about a single thing.

590
00:32:29,892 --> 00:32:32,783
He finally came to his senses. Good for him.

591
00:32:32,783 --> 00:32:35,440
The timing is just annoying.

592
00:32:35,440 --> 00:32:37,942
He acted like he didn't know all this time,
but why is he doing this now?

593
00:32:37,942 --> 00:32:41,716
What do you think?
It's all because his wife put him up to it.

594
00:32:41,716 --> 00:32:44,683
Oh, my poor son.
What am I going to do with my son now?

595
00:32:44,683 --> 00:32:46,976
Oh, Mom, enough with the "my son" routine.

596
00:32:46,976 --> 00:32:51,538
These days, it's not normal for one woman
to shoulder all the housework alone.

597
00:32:51,538 --> 00:32:54,681
While we're at it, let's get rid of
this outdated ancestral rite too, yeah?

598
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:55,855
Huh?

599
00:32:55,855 --> 00:32:57,239
Shut your mouth, you girl!

600
00:32:57,239 --> 00:32:58,916
Stay out of it.

601
00:32:58,916 --> 00:33:02,309
Hey, if you have a mouth, say something.

602
00:33:02,309 --> 00:33:04,372
Is that how your parents raised you?

603
00:33:04,372 --> 00:33:06,216
- Mom!
- Mom!

604
00:33:17,416 --> 00:33:21,084
Honey, put on your coat. Let's go home.

605
00:33:29,676 --> 00:33:32,264
Yul, be careful not to get hurt.

606
00:33:32,264 --> 00:33:33,964
Okay.

607
00:33:35,992 --> 00:33:39,576
Kwon Se Ah, who never cared
what anyone thought,

608
00:33:39,576 --> 00:33:41,676
is actually worried about what a kid thinks.

609
00:33:41,676 --> 00:33:44,349
Parenting is hard, indeed.

610
00:33:46,390 --> 00:33:48,396
I wonder if she's finally calmed down.

611
00:33:48,396 --> 00:33:50,542
What did you just say?

612
00:33:50,542 --> 00:33:51,649
We're not participating
in the ancestral rites anymore.

613
00:33:51,649 --> 00:33:53,872
What are you doing? I said put on your coat.

614
00:33:53,872 --> 00:33:55,768
What are you saying you won't do?

615
00:33:55,768 --> 00:33:57,383
- Oh, my.
- Mother!

616
00:33:57,383 --> 00:33:59,116
Mom, Mom...

617
00:34:00,532 --> 00:34:03,312
I think I was being short-sighted.

618
00:34:03,312 --> 00:34:06,256
I used to think
going along with everything you said

619
00:34:06,256 --> 00:34:10,224
was the best way to keep the peace,
but not anymore.

620
00:34:10,224 --> 00:34:16,060
Just as I'm your precious son,
she's my precious wife.

621
00:34:16,060 --> 00:34:19,780
Mom, I'm so scared that one day
she might suddenly disappear from my side.

622
00:34:19,780 --> 00:34:23,412
Just imagining it makes me
feel like I can't breathe.

623
00:34:23,412 --> 00:34:25,060
She is my precious family.

624
00:34:25,060 --> 00:34:29,383
So please, don't ever treat my wife
or my family that way again.

625
00:34:31,549 --> 00:34:35,649
- Unbelievable, that... that punk...
- Mom, Mom!

626
00:34:42,172 --> 00:34:43,872
This...

627
00:34:45,728 --> 00:34:47,583
Why am I...

628
00:34:50,272 --> 00:34:52,116
How did I...

629
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:55,283
Mother, I'm sorry.

630
00:34:55,283 --> 00:34:57,583
I'm sorry. I shouldn't be receiving this...

631
00:34:59,768 --> 00:35:02,640
Wait... Hey, Kwon Tae Seong!

632
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:04,349
Aren't you coming here?

633
00:35:04,349 --> 00:35:05,783
- Mom.
- Aren't you coming here?

634
00:35:05,783 --> 00:35:07,549
What are you really trying to do?

635
00:35:07,549 --> 00:35:09,383
- Apologize to your mom.
- What's wrong with you?

636
00:35:09,383 --> 00:35:10,483
And why are you acting like this too?

637
00:35:10,483 --> 00:35:11,683
You're just going to leave after this?

638
00:35:11,683 --> 00:35:13,016
Why are you picking up the dried pollock?

639
00:35:13,016 --> 00:35:14,349
You're just going to leave like this?

640
00:35:14,349 --> 00:35:16,780
- Hurry up and say you're sorry.
- You have no manners.

641
00:35:16,780 --> 00:35:18,136
Oh, stop.

642
00:35:18,136 --> 00:35:19,816
- Stop it!
- You dare?

643
00:35:19,816 --> 00:35:20,956
- You little punk!
- Mom?

644
00:35:20,956 --> 00:35:22,740
- Mom!
- Oh, my!

645
00:35:22,740 --> 00:35:23,749
Are you okay?

646
00:35:23,749 --> 00:35:24,949
You little...

647
00:35:24,949 --> 00:35:26,116
Stop it! No!

648
00:35:26,116 --> 00:35:27,916
You little punk!

649
00:35:29,888 --> 00:35:31,352
You little punk!

650
00:35:31,352 --> 00:35:32,572
Seriously, you...

651
00:35:32,572 --> 00:35:33,649
Hey, come here!

652
00:35:33,649 --> 00:35:34,683
[Pancake Mix]
Come here.

653
00:35:34,683 --> 00:35:36,288
You little punk!

654
00:35:36,288 --> 00:35:39,083
How dare you do this here?

655
00:35:58,416 --> 00:36:02,316
Well, I guess she's
the only person in the world

656
00:36:02,316 --> 00:36:03,636
who can actually chew Yoo Bo Na out.

657
00:36:03,636 --> 00:36:07,016
There's always something new
to learn and master.

658
00:36:07,016 --> 00:36:08,852
That's what running a household is like.

659
00:36:08,852 --> 00:36:11,449
You just have to break through
them again. What can you do?

660
00:36:11,449 --> 00:36:13,564
Just grind it out with sheer effort.

661
00:36:13,564 --> 00:36:17,283
Well, sometimes no amount of effort
can get you through something.

662
00:36:17,283 --> 00:36:21,249
Jeez, that old lady really never changes.

663
00:36:21,249 --> 00:36:24,356
It's about time she showed a bit of mercy.

664
00:36:24,356 --> 00:36:26,688
Will it get better as more time passes?

665
00:36:26,688 --> 00:36:30,916
Yeah, after all that rubbing
each other the wrong way,

666
00:36:31,545 --> 00:36:36,772
laughing and crying together,
physically clashing and hurting each other,

667
00:36:36,772 --> 00:36:39,728
time piles up until it becomes
that thick, sticky bond

668
00:36:39,728 --> 00:36:42,383
we call family.

669
00:36:45,048 --> 00:36:47,083
I guess that's why it's so hard.

670
00:36:49,565 --> 00:36:53,236
<i>Sometimes I find it fascinating,
and sometimes I'm jealous.</i>

671
00:36:53,236 --> 00:36:56,916
<i>Because I've never had anything like that.</i>

672
00:36:58,838 --> 00:37:01,776
Mom! Tae Seong!

673
00:37:01,776 --> 00:37:02,776
Tae Seong!

674
00:37:02,776 --> 00:37:06,249
Yul! Yul is missing!

675
00:37:07,956 --> 00:37:09,656
Bo Na...

676
00:37:10,764 --> 00:37:12,064
Yul!

677
00:37:12,064 --> 00:37:13,628
- Yul!
- Yul...

678
00:37:13,628 --> 00:37:15,580
- You look for her too! Hurry!
- Mom.

679
00:37:15,580 --> 00:37:16,580
Oh, she's not here.

680
00:37:16,580 --> 00:37:18,704
- Yul!
- Is she not there?

681
00:37:18,704 --> 00:37:19,932
- She's not there?
- No.

682
00:37:19,932 --> 00:37:22,204
- What do I do?
- Go check over there.

683
00:37:22,204 --> 00:37:24,016
Yul!

684
00:37:24,016 --> 00:37:25,848
Here? Was she here?

685
00:37:25,848 --> 00:37:27,516
Kwon Se Ah, are you sure you lost her here?

686
00:37:27,516 --> 00:37:33,299
Yeah! I was... I was sitting right here,
and Yul was playing over there.

687
00:37:33,299 --> 00:37:36,516
Chiba! Chiba's leash
came loose, and it ran off,

688
00:37:36,516 --> 00:37:41,083
so I went after it and came back,
but Yul was gone.

689
00:37:41,083 --> 00:37:43,283
Oh, seriously, this kid...

690
00:37:43,283 --> 00:37:44,788
- Yul!
- Oh, for goodness' sake.

691
00:37:44,788 --> 00:37:47,568
Come on, stop crying, you girl.
It's driving me crazy, seriously.

692
00:37:47,568 --> 00:37:50,020
Hey, you take her
and go back inside the house.

693
00:37:50,020 --> 00:37:53,200
Clean up the mess in there.

694
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:56,183
Mom, is that really what you say
to a mom who's just lost her child?

695
00:37:57,208 --> 00:37:59,672
Yeah, okay. Got it, Tae Seong.

696
00:37:59,672 --> 00:38:03,832
Yeah, when he gets there,
check the CCTV and call me.

697
00:38:03,832 --> 00:38:06,072
It's Tae Seong. He couldn't reach
the security guard earlier,

698
00:38:06,072 --> 00:38:07,952
but he just got through,
and the guard is on his way.

699
00:38:07,952 --> 00:38:11,396
Let's split up and search
the area for now, okay?

700
00:38:11,396 --> 00:38:12,596
Split up. Go.

701
00:38:12,596 --> 00:38:14,272
You go that way. I'll check over there.

702
00:38:14,272 --> 00:38:16,116
That way...

703
00:38:23,176 --> 00:38:24,312
Ms. Yoo!

704
00:38:24,312 --> 00:38:25,568
Oh, Assistant Manager Ki!

705
00:38:25,568 --> 00:38:27,324
You got here sooner than I expected.

706
00:38:27,324 --> 00:38:28,652
Thank you so much for coming.

707
00:38:28,652 --> 00:38:30,236
You said you lost a child, so...

708
00:38:30,236 --> 00:38:32,383
What do I do?

709
00:38:32,383 --> 00:38:33,948
- This...
- That one?

710
00:38:33,948 --> 00:38:37,152
Yeah, can you do it? Is it possible?

711
00:38:37,152 --> 00:38:40,772
So this is what it means
to feel chills and get goosebumps.

712
00:38:40,772 --> 00:38:42,616
I'm counting on you.

713
00:38:43,444 --> 00:38:45,351
Where on earth is she?

714
00:38:45,351 --> 00:38:47,483
Jeez, I'm going crazy.

715
00:38:49,260 --> 00:38:51,349
Oh, Bo Na...

716
00:38:56,272 --> 00:38:57,372
- Se Ah.
- Bo Na.

717
00:38:57,372 --> 00:38:58,844
Se Ah, what's the situation?

718
00:38:58,844 --> 00:39:00,220
Did you check Seo Yeon's place?

719
00:39:00,220 --> 00:39:02,016
Well, they said she never came there either.

720
00:39:02,016 --> 00:39:05,906
And... I didn't see her on the way here.

721
00:39:05,906 --> 00:39:10,549
I'm so sorry, Bo Na.
I should've been watching her better.

722
00:39:12,248 --> 00:39:13,449
We'll find her.

723
00:39:13,449 --> 00:39:16,108
Yul is a smart girl. She'll be okay.

724
00:39:16,108 --> 00:39:17,808
It's okay.

725
00:39:23,112 --> 00:39:26,356
But who is that?

726
00:39:26,356 --> 00:39:30,016
Oh, he's a coworker of mine.

727
00:39:30,016 --> 00:39:31,216
Hacking is his hobby,

728
00:39:31,216 --> 00:39:34,849
so I asked him to see if he could
access those CCTV cameras.

729
00:39:34,849 --> 00:39:38,117
And you know this
has to stay a secret, right?

730
00:39:38,117 --> 00:39:42,392
Yes, I've never met a hacker
in real life before.

731
00:39:42,392 --> 00:39:43,560
It's done.

732
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:45,749
Huh?

733
00:39:48,212 --> 00:39:50,352
What's the exact time the child went missing?

734
00:39:50,352 --> 00:39:54,083
Sometime between 6:30 p.m. and 7 p.m.

735
00:39:56,340 --> 00:39:58,040
I found her.

736
00:40:08,504 --> 00:40:12,749
Luckily, no one took her.
She left on her own.

737
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:15,340
Thank goodness.

738
00:40:16,388 --> 00:40:18,928
She seems to have wandered
around the apartment complex,

739
00:40:18,928 --> 00:40:24,048
then left the complex
and headed toward the main road.

740
00:40:24,048 --> 00:40:25,368
The main road?

741
00:40:25,368 --> 00:40:28,496
Then I'll check that way.
Let me know if you find anything.

742
00:40:28,496 --> 00:40:30,196
Oh...

743
00:40:35,304 --> 00:40:39,216
Were you the one
who was with her until the end?

744
00:40:41,012 --> 00:40:42,100
Yes.

745
00:40:42,100 --> 00:40:44,244
Do you remember anything?

746
00:40:44,244 --> 00:40:47,661
Anything strange about what she said or did?

747
00:40:47,661 --> 00:40:51,697
Oh, well...

748
00:40:51,697 --> 00:40:53,626
Take your time and think.

749
00:40:53,626 --> 00:40:57,349
Even the smallest thing could be a clue.

750
00:40:59,188 --> 00:41:04,128
Yul was asking me a lot of questions.

751
00:41:04,128 --> 00:41:06,668
Auntie, how do you get to heaven?

752
00:41:06,668 --> 00:41:08,536
Heaven? You have to die to go there.

753
00:41:08,536 --> 00:41:11,648
Die, die!

754
00:41:11,648 --> 00:41:16,157
Oh, no! I must've been crazy!

755
00:41:16,157 --> 00:41:20,249
She asked how to get to heaven.

756
00:41:20,249 --> 00:41:23,704
I told her you have to die.

757
00:41:23,704 --> 00:41:25,848
Oh, what do I do?

758
00:41:25,848 --> 00:41:27,349
Why would you say something like that?

759
00:41:27,349 --> 00:41:29,404
Well...

760
00:41:29,404 --> 00:41:33,906
Yul asked me what the ancestral rite is,

761
00:41:33,906 --> 00:41:39,316
and I told her people come down
from heaven to have a meal...

762
00:41:40,824 --> 00:41:42,749
Oh, my...

763
00:41:42,749 --> 00:41:45,932
This is all my fault.

764
00:41:45,932 --> 00:41:49,583
I was stupid enough
to take my eyes off my niece.

765
00:41:50,224 --> 00:41:54,092
Yul, I'm so sorry.

766
00:41:54,092 --> 00:41:57,088
Stop crying. I think I've found a clue.

767
00:41:57,088 --> 00:41:58,249
What?

768
00:41:58,249 --> 00:42:00,265
Yul going missing isn't your fault.

769
00:42:00,265 --> 00:42:03,683
So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.

770
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:15,436
Tae Seong!

771
00:42:15,436 --> 00:42:17,804
- Honey!
- Where's Yul?

772
00:42:17,804 --> 00:42:21,640
Well... We'll find Yul soon,
so I don't think you need to worry too much.

773
00:42:21,640 --> 00:42:24,416
Yul went toward the main road, right?

774
00:42:25,224 --> 00:42:27,716
How did you know...

775
00:42:27,716 --> 00:42:29,524
[Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do]

776
00:42:29,524 --> 00:42:31,716
Yeah, Assistant Manager Ki,
what did you find?

777
00:42:33,112 --> 00:42:34,812
What?

778
00:42:38,592 --> 00:42:40,400
She was looking up at the sky.

779
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:42,888
So there must've been something
in the sky, right?

780
00:42:42,888 --> 00:42:45,636
<i>Judging by the slight movement of her head,</i>

781
00:42:45,636 --> 00:42:47,304
<i>I think it might have been an airplane.</i>

782
00:42:47,304 --> 00:42:48,647
<i>Oh? That's right!</i>

783
00:42:48,647 --> 00:42:51,083
<i>Flights to Gimpo fly over our neighborhood.</i>

784
00:42:51,083 --> 00:42:52,900
Yul loves watching planes,

785
00:42:52,900 --> 00:42:56,160
so sometimes I take her up
to Tae Seong's rooftop...

786
00:42:56,160 --> 00:42:57,883
Oh, my!

787
00:43:03,420 --> 00:43:09,316
From what you said, it seems Yul
wanted to go to heaven for some reason.

788
00:43:36,184 --> 00:43:38,416
I'll get the key.

789
00:43:40,028 --> 00:43:41,728
Yeah.

790
00:43:44,583 --> 00:43:47,952
Take me with you!

791
00:43:47,952 --> 00:43:50,392
Take me with you!

792
00:43:50,392 --> 00:43:52,904
Take me with you too.

793
00:43:52,904 --> 00:43:56,228
Take me with you!

794
00:43:56,228 --> 00:43:59,115
Take me with you.

795
00:43:59,115 --> 00:44:04,069
Come here, and take me with you.

796
00:44:04,069 --> 00:44:07,783
<i>I think she thought the airplane
would take her there.</i>

797
00:44:09,656 --> 00:44:13,277
It was left open for waterproofing work
earlier today, but I locked it just now.

798
00:44:13,277 --> 00:44:17,149
Oh, my God. What on earth happened?

799
00:44:25,524 --> 00:44:27,264
Huh?

800
00:44:27,264 --> 00:44:30,716
Who told you to come up here alone? Huh?
Is that what I taught you?

801
00:44:30,716 --> 00:44:32,448
Are you going to wander around
by yourself at night like this?

802
00:44:32,448 --> 00:44:34,340
Why did you come up here
in the middle of the night?

803
00:44:34,340 --> 00:44:37,883
Are you hurt anywhere?
Are you going to do that again?

804
00:44:38,968 --> 00:44:41,608
I was going to bring them back.

805
00:44:41,608 --> 00:44:43,848
Who? Bring who back?

806
00:44:43,848 --> 00:44:46,516
Mommy's mom and dad.

807
00:44:47,380 --> 00:44:51,283
I heard they went to heaven.

808
00:44:53,208 --> 00:44:57,349
I was going to bring them back on a plane.

809
00:44:58,357 --> 00:45:01,576
Because Mommy is an orphan.

810
00:45:01,576 --> 00:45:05,516
I don't want Mommy to be an orphan.

811
00:45:17,552 --> 00:45:20,860
I see. I'm sorry. I...

812
00:45:20,860 --> 00:45:23,668
I didn't know how you felt
and scolded you first. I'm sorry.

813
00:45:23,668 --> 00:45:24,985
Don't cry, Yul. Come here.

814
00:45:24,985 --> 00:45:27,283
I'm sorry. Mommy's sorry.

815
00:45:28,792 --> 00:45:31,183
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have done that.

816
00:46:01,744 --> 00:46:02,936
Are you okay?

817
00:46:02,936 --> 00:46:04,636
Huh?

818
00:46:06,124 --> 00:46:08,212
I'm okay.

819
00:46:08,212 --> 00:46:10,974
Anyway, we found Yul safely.

820
00:46:10,974 --> 00:46:12,720
I'm sorry.

821
00:46:12,720 --> 00:46:16,164
But how could you do that to me?

822
00:46:16,164 --> 00:46:20,440
How could you imagine me
suddenly disappearing one day?

823
00:46:20,440 --> 00:46:22,416
How could you imagine such a thing?

824
00:46:23,240 --> 00:46:24,940
Huh?

825
00:46:26,692 --> 00:46:30,000
When you have something precious,
like an expensive jewel,

826
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:32,112
you're always afraid of losing it.

827
00:46:32,112 --> 00:46:34,411
That's what you are to me.

828
00:46:34,411 --> 00:46:37,183
You're so precious to me...

829
00:46:38,388 --> 00:46:40,749
that I'm afraid I'll lose you.

830
00:46:52,083 --> 00:46:56,468
I mean, you're not usually like this,
so why today...

831
00:46:56,468 --> 00:46:58,340
I don't know. You're in big trouble now.

832
00:46:58,340 --> 00:47:00,916
You totally lost points with Mother.

833
00:47:02,116 --> 00:47:05,949
Well, I can just earn double the points
I lost with Mom from you.

834
00:47:08,624 --> 00:47:11,984
No, I definitely lost a lot of points today.

835
00:47:11,984 --> 00:47:15,168
Because of me,
the ancestral rites were canceled.

836
00:47:15,168 --> 00:47:18,383
But we all decided that by vote, so whatever.

837
00:47:21,712 --> 00:47:24,656
Our Yul really did something big today.

838
00:47:24,656 --> 00:47:28,916
She even softened Grandma's stubborn heart.

839
00:47:28,916 --> 00:47:31,596
My daughter is better than I.

840
00:47:31,596 --> 00:47:34,349
She even comforted her mommy's heart.

841
00:47:38,304 --> 00:47:41,916
I'm supposed to be the one
comforting my daughter.

842
00:47:42,692 --> 00:47:45,894
She's still so young.

843
00:47:45,894 --> 00:47:49,549
I wish she didn't have to
understand things like that yet.

844
00:48:13,332 --> 00:48:15,032
Oh, dear.

845
00:48:16,060 --> 00:48:19,908
She's a mom too, so she went
completely crazy over her own kid.

846
00:48:19,908 --> 00:48:21,684
But still, that's too much.

847
00:48:21,684 --> 00:48:24,516
Still, how can she glare
at her mother-in-law like that?

848
00:48:26,244 --> 00:48:29,249
Because Mommy is an orphan.

849
00:48:30,257 --> 00:48:33,906
I don't want Mommy to be an orphan.

850
00:48:33,906 --> 00:48:35,920
Is it because she's an orphan?

851
00:48:35,920 --> 00:48:40,183
She does seem especially attached
when it comes to her family.

852
00:48:43,456 --> 00:48:45,249
Looks like...

853
00:48:47,181 --> 00:48:50,008
Bo Na is pretty athletic, huh?

854
00:48:50,008 --> 00:48:52,264
You little punk!

855
00:48:52,264 --> 00:48:53,980
No wonder.

856
00:48:53,980 --> 00:48:56,749
Did she do sports
or something back in school?

857
00:48:59,892 --> 00:49:02,700
But why has she been
spacing out since earlier?

858
00:49:02,700 --> 00:49:05,883
<i>So please don't cry. I'll find her for you.</i>

859
00:49:20,339 --> 00:49:21,520
What?

860
00:49:21,520 --> 00:49:23,220
What's wrong with her?

861
00:49:24,604 --> 00:49:27,416
She must still be shaken up from losing Yul.

862
00:49:29,894 --> 00:49:34,616
Anyway, I'm so relieved the ancestral rites
are over as of today!

863
00:49:35,257 --> 00:49:37,206
What an ungrateful bunch!

864
00:49:37,206 --> 00:49:39,644
You don't care about your mom one bit.

865
00:49:39,644 --> 00:49:42,628
Oh, our dear Ok Seon Ja, what's wrong now?

866
00:49:42,628 --> 00:49:45,149
If there's no ancestral rite,
you're the one who'll have it easiest.

867
00:49:45,149 --> 00:49:47,586
Easy for you to say.

868
00:49:47,586 --> 00:49:49,596
I've done this my whole life.

869
00:49:49,596 --> 00:49:53,673
If we abolish it now,
how am I supposed to face our ancestors?

870
00:49:53,673 --> 00:49:55,868
Oh, Mom!

871
00:49:55,868 --> 00:49:57,504
It's settled.
Why are you bringing it up again?

872
00:49:57,504 --> 00:50:02,220
We voted on whether to abolish it,
and the majority voted yes.

873
00:50:02,220 --> 00:50:04,316
That's it! Done! Over!

874
00:50:05,243 --> 00:50:09,156
Let's go clean up that mess over there.

875
00:50:09,156 --> 00:50:12,349
Oh, my, when are we ever
going to clean all that up?

876
00:50:13,124 --> 00:50:14,498
You godless bunch!

877
00:50:14,498 --> 00:50:18,716
Just you wait!
I'll do it all by myself next year.

878
00:50:29,896 --> 00:50:32,672
By the way, what was the vote count?

879
00:50:32,672 --> 00:50:34,148
- Huh?
- You counted the votes.

880
00:50:34,148 --> 00:50:36,392
You're the only one who saw the results.

881
00:50:36,392 --> 00:50:39,616
Well, obviously,
Mom was the one vote against it.

882
00:50:41,628 --> 00:50:43,583
That's...

883
00:50:53,684 --> 00:50:55,668
a secret.

884
00:50:55,668 --> 00:50:57,144
Why?

885
00:50:57,144 --> 00:50:58,916
Tell me, please.

886
00:50:58,916 --> 00:51:02,519
We agreed to keep the vote count secret.

887
00:51:02,519 --> 00:51:04,516
But tell me.

888
00:51:04,516 --> 00:51:06,966
Fine, I'm going to sulk.

889
00:51:06,966 --> 00:51:08,408
What's wrong?

890
00:51:08,408 --> 00:51:10,624
Please don't talk to me.

891
00:51:10,624 --> 00:51:14,216
And I don't think I'll get over this easily.

892
00:51:16,304 --> 00:51:19,528
Please tell me! Please!

893
00:51:19,528 --> 00:51:21,183
- Are you really that curious?
- Yeah.

894
00:51:21,183 --> 00:51:22,983
I guess you would be.

895
00:51:22,983 --> 00:51:25,283
Come on, really?

896
00:51:32,740 --> 00:51:34,849
Help me!

897
00:51:34,849 --> 00:51:37,149
Help me! Please, over here!

898
00:51:37,149 --> 00:51:38,883
I'm falling! Help me!

899
00:51:38,883 --> 00:51:40,583
Help me!

900
00:51:40,583 --> 00:51:43,083
Help me! Please!

901
00:51:54,569 --> 00:51:57,600
We've determined that Tak Jong Gu
spends his time going back and forth

902
00:51:57,600 --> 00:52:02,440
between the 22nd-floor VIP gaming room
and the 23rd-floor VIP suite.

903
00:52:02,440 --> 00:52:06,904
His dad has forbidden him from leaving,
so he can't go outside

904
00:52:06,904 --> 00:52:09,452
and takes care of everything
inside this building.

905
00:52:09,452 --> 00:52:12,631
And since the gaming room is a sealed,
windowless space,

906
00:52:12,631 --> 00:52:15,236
he can't be sniped from outside.

907
00:52:15,236 --> 00:52:18,996
So that means we'd have to target him
while he's inside his suite.

908
00:52:18,996 --> 00:52:20,696
The problem is that...

909
00:52:21,888 --> 00:52:26,328
Tak Jong Gu's room, 2305,
is on this side of the building.

910
00:52:26,328 --> 00:52:29,384
As you can see, the front window
has a completely open view.

911
00:52:29,384 --> 00:52:33,483
And the convention center next door
is almost directly opposite it.

912
00:52:34,132 --> 00:52:37,257
So there's no angle for a sniper shot.

913
00:52:37,257 --> 00:52:41,649
Then we'd have to lure him outside first.

914
00:52:41,649 --> 00:52:45,818
So the only way for us to get close is
through the 22nd-floor gaming room?

915
00:52:45,818 --> 00:52:47,944
<i>The 22nd-floor gaming room is for VIPs only,</i>

916
00:52:47,944 --> 00:52:50,540
<i>so ordinary guests can't access it.</i>

917
00:52:50,540 --> 00:52:55,249
<i>There is, however, one way
for ordinary guests to get in.</i>

918
00:52:56,116 --> 00:52:57,812
<i>Every day, the person</i>

919
00:52:57,812 --> 00:53:01,384
<i>who wins the most chips
in the first-floor public gaming room</i>

920
00:53:01,384 --> 00:53:03,405
<i>gets a pass to the VIP gaming room.</i>

921
00:53:03,405 --> 00:53:06,283
<i>It's basically a one-day pass.</i>

922
00:53:08,431 --> 00:53:11,608
So they expect you to win downstairs
and lose it all upstairs.

923
00:53:11,608 --> 00:53:14,544
We're barely covering
operating expenses this month.

924
00:53:14,544 --> 00:53:17,506
So, one of us just needs to
pose as a customer

925
00:53:17,506 --> 00:53:22,031
and to win that VIP pass.

926
00:53:22,031 --> 00:53:25,664
Tak Jong Gu mainly plays blackjack.

927
00:53:25,664 --> 00:53:27,949
Anyone here know how to play blackjack?

928
00:53:29,035 --> 00:53:30,484
I've never played blackjack before.

929
00:53:30,484 --> 00:53:31,612
Then what games have you played?

930
00:53:31,612 --> 00:53:32,785
One Card.

931
00:53:32,785 --> 00:53:33,924
One Card?

932
00:53:33,924 --> 00:53:35,192
Is that any fun?

933
00:53:35,192 --> 00:53:36,892
No one?

934
00:53:40,460 --> 00:53:44,183
Has anyone ever won money playing blackjack?

935
00:54:05,838 --> 00:54:10,580
In blackjack, the player whose cards
total 21 or come closest to 21 wins,

936
00:54:10,580 --> 00:54:12,772
giving the dealer and player
roughly equal odds.

937
00:54:12,772 --> 00:54:16,449
So I created a program
that maximizes those odds.

938
00:54:17,593 --> 00:54:20,128
These glasses have the program
built into them.

939
00:54:20,128 --> 00:54:22,252
They recognize the cards that
have been played and those remaining,

940
00:54:22,252 --> 00:54:26,416
<i>and then signal whether I should
hit or stay with lights only I can see.</i>

941
00:54:35,690 --> 00:54:38,996
Congratulations.
This is your pass to the VIP gaming room.

942
00:54:38,996 --> 00:54:40,696
Thank you.

943
00:54:50,756 --> 00:54:54,416
<i>So we'll get the VIP pass
this way, go upstairs,</i>

944
00:54:55,423 --> 00:54:57,130
<i>and approach Tak Jong Gu.</i>

945
00:54:57,130 --> 00:55:00,716
<i>We'll drop a pill into his drink.</i>

946
00:55:01,388 --> 00:55:03,212
It's a drug that causes vasculitis.

947
00:55:03,212 --> 00:55:07,820
<i>A few minutes after he takes it,
red spots will break out all over his body.</i>

948
00:55:07,820 --> 00:55:09,504
Get a doctor now!

949
00:55:09,504 --> 00:55:11,896
Get the doctor!

950
00:55:11,896 --> 00:55:15,360
<i>That's when Manager Go will appear
disguised as the on-site doctor.</i>

951
00:55:15,360 --> 00:55:17,472
Hey! What's this?

952
00:55:17,472 --> 00:55:18,860
It's an acute allergic reaction.

953
00:55:18,860 --> 00:55:20,728
You could go into shock
if we leave you like this.

954
00:55:20,728 --> 00:55:22,816
We need to get you to a hospital right away.

955
00:55:26,824 --> 00:55:29,283
<i>Once we get Tak Jong Gu outside, we're done.</i>

956
00:55:51,183 --> 00:55:54,448
[Hongseon Rest Area]

957
00:55:54,448 --> 00:55:56,576
He didn't fall while working,

958
00:55:56,576 --> 00:55:59,856
so why was he there in the middle
of the night, and how did he fall?

959
00:55:59,856 --> 00:56:03,156
And from the exact same spot
where Kang Yeong Ho fell to his death.

960
00:56:03,156 --> 00:56:05,352
What does the police say?

961
00:56:05,352 --> 00:56:07,160
Looks like they don't have
any answers either.

962
00:56:07,160 --> 00:56:09,988
It was late at night in a remote area,
so there were no witnesses.

963
00:56:09,988 --> 00:56:12,292
Wow, but that Park Chun Bok guy,

964
00:56:12,292 --> 00:56:14,920
he acted like such a saint
during the interview.

965
00:56:14,920 --> 00:56:16,798
But he had assault, theft,
and even attempted murder on his record.

966
00:56:16,798 --> 00:56:19,796
A whopping five-time ex-con!

967
00:56:19,796 --> 00:56:22,788
You really can't judge a person
by appearances.

968
00:56:22,788 --> 00:56:27,556
And before he died, he was handing out money
from some unknown source?

969
00:56:27,556 --> 00:56:31,185
This feels like a terrifying case
involving Chairman Cheon Seong Gil,

970
00:56:31,185 --> 00:56:32,508
the field workers, and everyone in between.

971
00:56:32,508 --> 00:56:35,904
It seems like a complex and terrifying case.

972
00:56:35,904 --> 00:56:38,165
Anyway, Chairman Cheon Seong Gil
is at the center of it.

973
00:56:38,165 --> 00:56:40,283
Let's go meet him first.

974
00:56:41,536 --> 00:56:44,380
Do you think he'll see us?
He already refused our interview.

975
00:56:44,380 --> 00:56:46,636
Who says we have to do a formal interview?

976
00:56:46,636 --> 00:56:48,336
Oh!

977
00:56:55,596 --> 00:56:57,340
Seven.

978
00:56:57,340 --> 00:56:59,535
Hit.

979
00:56:59,535 --> 00:57:01,249
Thirteen.

980
00:57:05,350 --> 00:57:07,083
Stay.

981
00:57:08,096 --> 00:57:09,168
Fourteen.

982
00:57:09,168 --> 00:57:11,216
Twenty-four, bust.

983
00:57:17,296 --> 00:57:18,996
Eighteen.

984
00:57:20,116 --> 00:57:21,816
Stay.

985
00:57:35,760 --> 00:57:37,483
Eleven.

986
00:57:39,428 --> 00:57:41,448
- Down.
- Double down.

987
00:57:41,448 --> 00:57:43,356
[Double Down: Double your bet
and get one more card]

988
00:57:44,922 --> 00:57:46,516
Twenty-three. Dealer bust.

989
00:57:46,516 --> 00:57:48,428
[Bust: The total exceeds 21]

990
00:57:48,428 --> 00:57:50,365
Twenty-one.

991
00:57:50,365 --> 00:57:53,716
Congratulations. Your double down paid off.

992
00:57:56,106 --> 00:57:57,580
- Nice, blackjack!
- Blackjack!

993
00:57:57,580 --> 00:57:58,968
Congratulations!

994
00:57:58,968 --> 00:58:00,649
Would you like to take even money?

995
00:58:00,649 --> 00:58:01,884
[Even Money: If the dealer
might also have blackjack,]

996
00:58:01,884 --> 00:58:03,124
[you give up the 1.5:1 payout
and take 1:1 instead. A kind of insurance]

997
00:58:03,124 --> 00:58:04,880
Sure.

998
00:58:04,880 --> 00:58:07,308
Oh, come on.

999
00:58:07,308 --> 00:58:09,583
Don't do that.

1000
00:58:10,900 --> 00:58:13,628
You've got to go for it here,
even if you might lose.

1001
00:58:13,628 --> 00:58:16,416
Are you new to gambling?

1002
00:58:21,792 --> 00:58:23,452
Eighteen.

1003
00:58:23,452 --> 00:58:25,949
See? You barely won anything.

1004
00:58:25,949 --> 00:58:29,216
Making pennies like that,
when are you ever going to get rich?

1005
00:58:31,916 --> 00:58:35,435
Still, that's a decent win
for someone so chicken-hearted, huh?

1006
00:58:35,435 --> 00:58:38,216
Would you like to join the game, ma'am?

1007
00:58:39,140 --> 00:58:41,223
Me?

1008
00:58:41,223 --> 00:58:43,586
Oh, jeez.

1009
00:58:43,586 --> 00:58:46,616
I really shouldn't do this.

1010
00:58:47,868 --> 00:58:51,449
I really quit gambling.

1011
00:58:59,516 --> 00:59:01,349
[Gaecheon Construction]

1012
00:59:04,912 --> 00:59:09,316
Huh? Isn't that Chairman Cheon's car?

1013
00:59:21,580 --> 00:59:24,316
Looks like he's going somewhere.
What do we do?

1014
00:59:25,528 --> 00:59:28,740
What do you mean? We have to follow him.

1015
00:59:28,740 --> 00:59:30,449
Again?

1016
00:59:35,360 --> 00:59:36,416
Seventeen.

1017
00:59:36,416 --> 00:59:37,965
- Yes!
- Wow!

1018
00:59:37,965 --> 00:59:40,083
How many wins is that?

1019
00:59:48,196 --> 00:59:51,055
It's been so long
since I've felt this thrill.

1020
00:59:51,055 --> 00:59:54,616
Okay, from now on,

1021
00:59:54,616 --> 00:59:56,856
[Three Hands: One person plays three hands]
should I go three hands?

1022
00:59:56,856 --> 00:59:59,706
- Join?
- I'm good.

1023
00:59:59,706 --> 01:00:01,204
Chicken.

1024
01:00:01,204 --> 01:00:03,483
[Pair: First two cards have the same value]
I'm betting on a pair too.

1025
01:00:04,696 --> 01:00:06,483
No more bets?

1026
01:00:15,016 --> 01:00:17,040
Nice pair.

1027
01:00:17,040 --> 01:00:18,740
Yes!

1028
01:00:20,864 --> 01:00:23,106
Yeah.

1029
01:00:23,106 --> 01:00:24,176
Congratulations!

1030
01:00:24,176 --> 01:00:26,888
This is a pass granting
you access to the VIP gaming room.

1031
01:00:26,888 --> 01:00:29,848
Wow, thank you!

1032
01:00:29,848 --> 01:00:32,469
Thank you! Thank you!

1033
01:00:32,469 --> 01:00:34,216
Thank you!

1034
01:00:41,526 --> 01:00:43,464
Good job, chicken.

1035
01:00:43,464 --> 01:00:45,504
You should quit while you're ahead.

1036
01:00:45,504 --> 01:00:48,349
You'll lose everything otherwise.

1037
01:00:52,052 --> 01:00:53,144
See you around!

1038
01:00:59,248 --> 01:01:01,543
Oh, I lost!

1039
01:01:01,543 --> 01:01:03,981
I lost again!

1040
01:01:03,981 --> 01:01:06,620
Mister, I lost again.

1041
01:01:06,620 --> 01:01:09,716
I lost again!

1042
01:01:11,636 --> 01:01:13,336
What are you doing here again?

1043
01:01:16,081 --> 01:01:18,156
Even your plans fail sometimes.

1044
01:01:18,156 --> 01:01:20,216
I'm sorry, Ms. Yoo.

1045
01:01:23,557 --> 01:01:27,344
But there are always
unexpected variables in the field.

1046
01:01:27,344 --> 01:01:31,353
And cleaning up after a junior's mistakes
is part of being a good senior.

1047
01:01:31,353 --> 01:01:33,649
What are you thinking?

1048
01:01:33,649 --> 01:01:34,892
I'm thinking maybe I should go in directly.

1049
01:01:34,892 --> 01:01:36,984
You, personally?

1050
01:01:36,984 --> 01:01:38,156
The gaming room might be difficult,

1051
01:01:38,156 --> 01:01:40,692
but wouldn't it be easier
to sneak into his suite?

1052
01:01:40,692 --> 01:01:42,880
I'll just drug his water and get out.

1053
01:01:42,880 --> 01:01:45,120
That's our best option right now.

1054
01:01:45,120 --> 01:01:46,544
I can't agree to that.

1055
01:01:46,544 --> 01:01:48,549
It's too dangerous for you
to expose yourself on-site.

1056
01:01:48,549 --> 01:01:51,412
You will back me up, won't you?

1057
01:01:51,412 --> 01:01:52,628
- Well, that's...
- Tell Manager Go

1058
01:01:52,628 --> 01:01:55,483
about the revised plan beforehand.

1059
01:01:57,224 --> 01:01:59,604
Okay, shall we go?

1060
01:01:59,604 --> 01:02:01,304
Ms. Yoo.

1061
01:02:02,288 --> 01:02:05,283
You know your safety comes first, right?

1062
01:02:12,676 --> 01:02:14,183
No, wait a moment.

1063
01:02:14,183 --> 01:02:15,531
Chairman!

1064
01:02:15,531 --> 01:02:19,883
Please, just let me in for a moment!

1065
01:02:19,883 --> 01:02:21,144
Oh, please!

1066
01:02:21,144 --> 01:02:23,116
Just a moment.

1067
01:03:10,740 --> 01:03:11,924
How bad is this guy?

1068
01:03:11,924 --> 01:03:14,316
On the surface,
it looks like an accidental mishap,

1069
01:03:14,316 --> 01:03:16,044
but a premeditated murder underneath?

1070
01:03:16,044 --> 01:03:18,342
- Done.
- Someone's coming down the hall.

1071
01:03:18,342 --> 01:03:19,352
A reporter?

1072
01:03:19,352 --> 01:03:21,772
Well, this just got interesting.

1073
01:03:21,772 --> 01:03:24,164
No, it's too dangerous for you
to meet him there yourself.

1074
01:03:24,164 --> 01:03:25,894
That woman could become a witness...

1075
01:03:25,894 --> 01:03:27,423
What's the variable this time?

1076
01:03:27,423 --> 01:03:28,773
Someone else is coming down the hall.

1077
01:03:28,773 --> 01:03:30,816
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo!

1078
01:03:30,816 --> 01:03:33,788
In the end, the day will come
when that secret is revealed.

1079
01:03:33,788 --> 01:03:35,981
It's all my fault.

1080
01:03:35,981 --> 01:03:39,483
Calm down. Director Yoo will be fine.

1081
01:03:40,100 --> 01:03:41,236
What's wrong?

1082
01:03:41,236 --> 01:03:43,216
It's someone I know.

1083
01:03:45,440 --> 01:03:47,440
MkvDrama.Net
